# React Component Conventions

Follow existing patterns. Do not introduce new patterns.

## Atoms vs Connected

- **atoms/** — Presentational only. No `getContextStores`. Receives data via props.
- **connected/** — Uses `getContextStores()`, selectors, and actions.

## Component Shape

- Functional components only
- Use `FC<Props>` or explicit prop types
- `interface Props { ... }` above component
- Default export for components
- Barrel exports via `components/atoms/index.ts`

## Connected Component Pattern

```tsx
const MyComponent: FC<Props> = ({ title }) => {
  const contextStores = getContextStores();
  const { featureState, assetManagerDispatch } = contextStores;
  const data = getSelectorName(contextStores);

  const handler = () => {
    someAction(assetManagerId, payload, assetManagerDispatch);
  };
  // ...
};
```

## Atoms Pattern

```tsx
interface Props {
  title: string;
  onAction?: () => void;
}

const MyAtom: FC<Props> = ({ title, onAction }) => {
  return (/* JSX */);
};

export default MyAtom;
```

## UI and Forms

- Use **Ant Design** components (Select, Modal, Table, etc.) instead of custom ones
- Use **ModalForm** from `components/atoms/ModalForm` for form modals
- Hooks at top level; extract complex logic to custom hooks when needed

